1
00:00:01,210 --> 00:00:03,500
[♪ opening theme song playing]

2
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:14,810
DAEMONS OF THE SHADOW REALM

3
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:32,430
[birds chirping]

4
00:01:36,640 --> 00:01:38,020
[ASAGIRI] They found us.

5
00:01:38,060 --> 00:01:41,230
But we know the way
to enter Tadera's hideout now.

6
00:01:41,770 --> 00:01:44,770
So we may recover the remains
of those who once served us,

7
00:01:44,810 --> 00:01:46,230
the ones who went missing.

8
00:01:46,900 --> 00:01:49,480
That will suffice, Asagiri.

9
00:01:49,530 --> 00:01:52,070
BIG BROTHER AND LITTLE BROTHER

10
00:02:01,580 --> 00:02:04,710
[YURU] I noticed something when
I was running around earlier.

11
00:02:06,170 --> 00:02:08,250
Their attacks were relentless.

12
00:02:08,290 --> 00:02:10,760
Except for when
I hid behind this spot.

13
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:12,800
♪

14
00:02:18,850 --> 00:02:19,970
They're here.

15
00:02:20,810 --> 00:02:22,980
Tenaga-Ashinaga's master.

16
00:02:28,150 --> 00:02:29,270
Come on out.

17
00:02:29,320 --> 00:02:31,740
[BOY] But are you gonna
kill me if I do?

18
00:02:31,780 --> 00:02:33,740
[gasps] That's a young voice.

19
00:02:33,780 --> 00:02:35,280
Is it a kid?

20
00:02:35,320 --> 00:02:37,410
[YURU] Your fate depends
on what you say.

21
00:02:37,450 --> 00:02:39,160
[WOMAN] No mercy.

22
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:41,410
Hard to believe he's a kid, too.

23
00:02:41,450 --> 00:02:43,290
[rustling]

24
00:02:43,660 --> 00:02:45,500
[whimpering softly]

25
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:49,750
I'll answer
any question you have!

26
00:02:49,790 --> 00:02:52,300
Please, just spare my life!
I don't wanna die!

27
00:02:52,340 --> 00:02:53,840
You've gotta be joking.

28
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:55,880
This brat's
barely out of diapers!

29
00:02:55,930 --> 00:02:57,760
Are you Tenaga-Ashinaga's
master?

30
00:02:57,800 --> 00:03:00,510
Yes, I am.
Or I guess, I was.

31
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:02,180
What are you doing here, kiddo?

32
00:03:02,770 --> 00:03:04,060
You got a name?

33
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:06,150
I'm sorry to intrude.

34
00:03:06,190 --> 00:03:07,600
I'm Ken Tadera.

35
00:03:07,650 --> 00:03:08,650
I believe...

36
00:03:08,770 --> 00:03:11,190
-my father owns this house?
-[ALL] Uh?

37
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:13,570
[YURU] Mmm?

38
00:03:14,650 --> 00:03:16,240
Run that one by me again.

39
00:03:16,740 --> 00:03:18,450
[YURU] You said your dad?

40
00:03:18,490 --> 00:03:20,240
So this is your son, Dera?

41
00:03:20,280 --> 00:03:21,870
No, no, slow down, buddy!

42
00:03:21,910 --> 00:03:23,750
There's no way I...

43
00:03:25,870 --> 00:03:27,830
[Dera grunts softly]

44
00:03:28,830 --> 00:03:30,000
I don't know this kid!

45
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:31,500
That pause was awful pregnant.

46
00:03:31,540 --> 00:03:33,920
Your mother!
Is she from Japan?

47
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:35,210
We're both from Ethiopia!

48
00:03:35,260 --> 00:03:36,680
And what's her name?

49
00:03:36,720 --> 00:03:38,090
It's Abeba Tesfaye!

50
00:03:38,130 --> 00:03:41,300
Yep! I 100% haven't heard
that name before!

51
00:03:41,350 --> 00:03:42,600
This kid isn't mine!

52
00:03:42,640 --> 00:03:46,730
Sorry, but are you Ryu Tadera,
by any chance?

53
00:03:46,770 --> 00:03:49,020
Dad told me
some stories about you.

54
00:03:49,060 --> 00:03:51,230
I'm Ken Tadera,
the son of Roei.

55
00:03:51,270 --> 00:03:52,520
It's nice to meet you.

56
00:03:52,570 --> 00:03:53,860
[Dera gasps softly]

57
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:55,280
Wait, Roei?

58
00:03:55,320 --> 00:03:57,860
I feel like I know that name
from a while back.

59
00:03:57,910 --> 00:03:59,820
[DERA]
That's my predecessor's name.

60
00:03:59,870 --> 00:04:01,490
And also my pop's.

61
00:04:01,820 --> 00:04:03,620
It makes sense
you'd remember him.

62
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:05,540
He did my job
when you were a kid.

63
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:06,660
So, you've met him.

64
00:04:06,710 --> 00:04:08,660
Wait, we have the same father?

65
00:04:08,710 --> 00:04:09,920
How old are you?

66
00:04:09,960 --> 00:04:11,000
I'm 13.

67
00:04:11,040 --> 00:04:13,500
So we're 22 years apart?

68
00:04:13,540 --> 00:04:15,880
How nice to see
long-lost half-brothers

69
00:04:15,920 --> 00:04:16,920
find each other!

70
00:04:16,960 --> 00:04:18,800
'Tis a moving chance reunion!

71
00:04:18,840 --> 00:04:20,470
Hey, that's great, Dera!

72
00:04:20,510 --> 00:04:21,850
Your family's gotten bigger!

73
00:04:21,890 --> 00:04:24,390
I'm sorry, am I supposed
to find this heartwarming?

74
00:04:24,430 --> 00:04:27,180
So, listen,
I accidentally overheard

75
00:04:27,230 --> 00:04:29,100
some of your conversation
from before.

76
00:04:29,140 --> 00:04:30,940
This guy with the blonde hair...

77
00:04:30,980 --> 00:04:33,810
Didn't you say he's one of the
twins from Higashi Village?

78
00:04:33,860 --> 00:04:35,690
So he must be
Mine and Nagisa's son.

79
00:04:35,730 --> 00:04:38,400
-[YURU] Uh?
-[KEN] Dad told me about them.

80
00:04:38,690 --> 00:04:41,320
Hold on. Are you saying
you know my mom and dad?

81
00:04:41,360 --> 00:04:43,910
I don't think I'd go that far.

82
00:04:44,530 --> 00:04:45,990
But they needed someone
to teach them

83
00:04:46,040 --> 00:04:47,910
how to escape
Higashi's barrier,

84
00:04:47,950 --> 00:04:49,500
and my dad agreed to help.

85
00:04:49,540 --> 00:04:50,670
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

86
00:04:50,830 --> 00:04:53,290
My old man did what now?
He never told me that!

87
00:04:53,330 --> 00:04:55,420
You're serious?
You've got one chance!

88
00:04:55,460 --> 00:04:56,750
If you know
where my parents are,

89
00:04:56,800 --> 00:04:58,340
-then tell me!
-[Ken screams]

90
00:04:58,380 --> 00:05:00,220
Please don't kill me! [cries]

91
00:05:00,260 --> 00:05:01,430
[WOMAN] Rough for you.

92
00:05:01,590 --> 00:05:04,100
The twin's parents ran away
from Higashi Village

93
00:05:04,140 --> 00:05:05,560
and joined the Kagemoris.

94
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:06,930
If your dad helped them,

95
00:05:06,970 --> 00:05:09,180
kinda makes it seem like
the Taderas are working

96
00:05:09,230 --> 00:05:11,020
-as Kagemori spies.
-[Dera exclaims]

97
00:05:11,060 --> 00:05:12,310
You're right.

98
00:05:12,350 --> 00:05:14,650
Uh, I should explain some more.

99
00:05:14,690 --> 00:05:16,820
[WOMAN] Nope, not another word
out of you!

100
00:05:16,860 --> 00:05:18,320
I've already heard
too much stuff

101
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:19,900
I got no business knowing!

102
00:05:19,940 --> 00:05:22,070
Look, you lot saved my life.

103
00:05:22,110 --> 00:05:24,990
So I'll return the favor
by keeping my mouth shut!

104
00:05:25,030 --> 00:05:27,120
Asuma won't be hearing
about this kid.

105
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:29,120
And I'm not gonna
try to sell this info

106
00:05:29,160 --> 00:05:30,960
as a tip to Higashi Village,
either!

107
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:32,420
Much appreciated.

108
00:05:32,460 --> 00:05:34,880
[WOMAN] With that said,
you gonna kill me,

109
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:36,250
or can I leave now?

110
00:05:36,420 --> 00:05:39,840
[Dera sighs] Asuma's daemon
did manage to track us here.

111
00:05:39,880 --> 00:05:41,340
So the route's
already out there,

112
00:05:41,380 --> 00:05:43,720
and this place is
all but useless to me.

113
00:05:44,180 --> 00:05:47,220
That means offing you now
isn't gonna do me any good.

114
00:05:47,260 --> 00:05:48,810
So I don't care.

115
00:05:48,850 --> 00:05:50,100
What do you think, Yuru?

116
00:05:50,140 --> 00:05:51,430
Why ask me?

117
00:05:51,480 --> 00:05:52,810
[DERA] This old bag...
[clears throat]

118
00:05:52,850 --> 00:05:55,310
This lady, she tried
to rat you out

119
00:05:55,350 --> 00:05:57,610
to Tenaga-Ashinaga
during the fight.

120
00:05:57,650 --> 00:05:59,190
[YURU] Oh, that? It's fine.

121
00:05:59,230 --> 00:06:01,740
I didn't feel like
she wanted to kill us.

122
00:06:01,780 --> 00:06:03,070
[WOMAN]
The kid's only got beef

123
00:06:03,110 --> 00:06:05,360
with people who actively
want him dead?

124
00:06:05,410 --> 00:06:06,870
That's shortsighted.

125
00:06:06,910 --> 00:06:09,540
Is your husband
in this line of work?

126
00:06:09,580 --> 00:06:12,910
Nah. Tried to settle down
with an ordinary civil servant.

127
00:06:12,960 --> 00:06:14,790
He doesn't know
the stuff I do on the side,

128
00:06:14,830 --> 00:06:15,960
and I don't want him to.

129
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:18,590
Well, I think it's safe
to let her walk away.

130
00:06:18,630 --> 00:06:20,500
I'm cool with it
as long as you are.

131
00:06:20,550 --> 00:06:21,880
[woman sighs]

132
00:06:22,510 --> 00:06:25,300
[WOMAN]
What upstanding gentlemen.

133
00:06:29,100 --> 00:06:30,180
Poor guys.

134
00:06:30,510 --> 00:06:32,480
Always wondered what happened
to the Kagemori agents

135
00:06:32,520 --> 00:06:35,140
who went missing after being
sent to tail a Tadera.

136
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:38,190
I know that's not
how I'd wanna go.

137
00:06:38,900 --> 00:06:40,230
Before I leave,

138
00:06:40,270 --> 00:06:42,150
would you mind
letting me bury the guys

139
00:06:42,190 --> 00:06:44,320
who came with me so they're
not just lying out here?

140
00:06:44,360 --> 00:06:48,120
I mean, they got no family
to hold a funeral for them.

141
00:06:48,160 --> 00:06:49,870
Sure, have at it.

142
00:06:49,910 --> 00:06:51,490
Just put 'em wherever you want.

143
00:06:51,540 --> 00:06:52,660
I'll help you.

144
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:55,960
You were talking about
killing me so casually.

145
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:58,170
Now you're gonna help
your enemy bury the dead?

146
00:06:58,880 --> 00:07:02,090
I gotta say, kid, your ethics
are all over the place.

147
00:07:02,130 --> 00:07:04,300
You always need
to bury the dead.

148
00:07:04,340 --> 00:07:05,880
Otherwise, you risk a plague.

149
00:07:06,380 --> 00:07:08,180
Something like that
can wipe out a village

150
00:07:08,220 --> 00:07:09,680
in the blink of an eye.

151
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:12,220
[WOMAN]
Oh. So that's how he lived.

152
00:07:12,770 --> 00:07:14,640
[YURU] Besides,
the sooner you're gone,

153
00:07:14,680 --> 00:07:16,390
the sooner we can talk to Ken.

154
00:07:16,890 --> 00:07:18,980
Hey, Left and Right,
mind lending a hand?

155
00:07:19,020 --> 00:07:20,520
[Right grunting]

156
00:07:23,400 --> 00:07:25,030
-[woman stammers]
-[Right chuckles]

157
00:07:25,070 --> 00:07:26,950
So does this look deep enough
for your needs?

158
00:07:26,990 --> 00:07:29,490
Oh, I didn't mean
"a hand" literally.

159
00:07:29,530 --> 00:07:31,450
But whatever works.

160
00:07:31,870 --> 00:07:33,160
[Ken exhales softly]

161
00:07:33,620 --> 00:07:34,950
So, uh...

162
00:07:35,500 --> 00:07:37,540
-Brother--
-[DERA] Call me Ryu.

163
00:07:38,130 --> 00:07:39,210
[KEN] All right.

164
00:07:39,250 --> 00:07:41,210
Then, Mr. Ryu...

165
00:07:41,250 --> 00:07:43,710
Thanks for beating those
scary daemons for me.

166
00:07:43,750 --> 00:07:45,300
You really saved my butt there.

167
00:07:45,340 --> 00:07:46,460
[Dera exhales softly]

168
00:07:48,470 --> 00:07:49,550
[YURU] Oh, yeah.

169
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:51,430
I know you can form
a contract with a daemon

170
00:07:51,470 --> 00:07:52,850
using your own blood.

171
00:07:52,890 --> 00:07:54,720
But what happens
if you want out?

172
00:07:54,770 --> 00:07:56,390
Is there a peaceful way
you can dissolve

173
00:07:56,440 --> 00:07:57,560
an unwanted contract?

174
00:07:57,810 --> 00:08:00,360
The contract's void
as long as all parties agree.

175
00:08:00,400 --> 00:08:02,770
Then everything goes back
to the way it was.

176
00:08:02,820 --> 00:08:04,110
[YURU] So they talk it out?

177
00:08:04,230 --> 00:08:06,940
Uh-huh. The master-servant thing
is for convenience.

178
00:08:06,990 --> 00:08:08,740
In reality, we're all equal.

179
00:08:08,780 --> 00:08:11,870
[BUNBUN] We've got feelings
of our own, mister.

180
00:08:12,530 --> 00:08:13,910
I get it.

181
00:08:13,950 --> 00:08:15,370
And in that case...

182
00:08:15,910 --> 00:08:17,160
Is it the same for us?

183
00:08:17,200 --> 00:08:18,250
Indeed.

184
00:08:18,290 --> 00:08:19,830
If you so desired,

185
00:08:19,920 --> 00:08:22,790
we would return to being statues
at Higashi Village's entrance.

186
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:24,550
And though our current contract

187
00:08:24,590 --> 00:08:27,010
isn't completely
without limitations,

188
00:08:27,050 --> 00:08:29,720
I will admit we're happy being
able to move about.

189
00:08:29,760 --> 00:08:31,350
We would rather stay like this.

190
00:08:31,390 --> 00:08:32,890
'Twas four hundred years.

191
00:08:32,930 --> 00:08:34,640
There is much yet to see
in this new world

192
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:36,310
before returning to our post.

193
00:08:36,350 --> 00:08:38,270
-[RIGHT] Listen, child.
-[Ken yelps]

194
00:08:38,310 --> 00:08:41,230
Not all daemons you will meet
are as kind-hearted as us,

195
00:08:41,270 --> 00:08:43,060
nor half so amenable to reason.

196
00:08:43,110 --> 00:08:45,150
To carelessly free
strange daemons

197
00:08:45,190 --> 00:08:46,570
is to invite your own doom.

198
00:08:46,610 --> 00:08:48,570
[KEN] I know I messed up!
[whimpers]

199
00:08:48,610 --> 00:08:51,870
Huh. I recall you said the power
of Seal is dangerous.

200
00:08:51,910 --> 00:08:53,990
But reflect now
on moments like these,

201
00:08:54,030 --> 00:08:55,450
where you could seal
a wicked daemon

202
00:08:55,490 --> 00:08:56,830
without any contract!

203
00:08:56,870 --> 00:08:58,540
Should Break be used instead,

204
00:08:58,580 --> 00:09:00,210
it would create a stray daemon.

205
00:09:00,250 --> 00:09:01,830
But Seal merely
locks them away

206
00:09:01,880 --> 00:09:03,580
into their relic,
safe and sound.

207
00:09:03,630 --> 00:09:06,210
In some ways, it's a kindness.

208
00:09:09,300 --> 00:09:10,470
[woman gasps]

209
00:09:11,130 --> 00:09:12,800
[WOMAN] Back just like that.

210
00:09:13,970 --> 00:09:16,260
[DERA] Feels like you
never even left, yeah?

211
00:09:16,310 --> 00:09:17,850
You good to make it home?

212
00:09:17,890 --> 00:09:19,850
[WOMAN] Yeah, sure.

213
00:09:20,180 --> 00:09:21,310
[DERA] Oh...

214
00:09:21,980 --> 00:09:24,150
Give Asuma my love,
won't you?

215
00:09:24,190 --> 00:09:25,560
From the heart.

216
00:09:25,770 --> 00:09:27,320
[door closes]

217
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:28,940
[bird cawing]

218
00:09:28,990 --> 00:09:30,320
[woman sighs]

219
00:09:31,990 --> 00:09:34,990
[WOMAN]
I think I'm ready to retire.

220
00:09:42,250 --> 00:09:44,290
[DERA] With her gone...

221
00:09:44,830 --> 00:09:46,210
You're up, Ken.

222
00:09:46,250 --> 00:09:48,750
Why don't you go ahead
and give us any info you got?

223
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:51,470
First, I wanna make it clear
I have no idea

224
00:09:51,510 --> 00:09:52,800
where Yuru's parents are
at all.

225
00:09:52,840 --> 00:09:54,260
[Yuru groans softly]

226
00:09:54,300 --> 00:09:56,970
[KEN] I wish I did,
but I don't even know

227
00:09:57,010 --> 00:09:59,470
where my own dad is,
let alone his.

228
00:09:59,520 --> 00:10:00,640
No kidding.

229
00:10:00,730 --> 00:10:02,560
Wonder if the old man's
kicked the bucket.

230
00:10:02,600 --> 00:10:05,400
Huh? I was kinda
hoping you would know

231
00:10:05,440 --> 00:10:07,070
something about
where I could find him.

232
00:10:07,110 --> 00:10:08,070
Sorry, buddy.

233
00:10:08,520 --> 00:10:10,900
Didn't you call him
your predecessor earlier?

234
00:10:11,240 --> 00:10:12,570
I figured he was already dead

235
00:10:12,610 --> 00:10:14,200
if you were
referring to him like that.

236
00:10:14,240 --> 00:10:16,490
[DERA] Don't go puttin' words
in my mouth.

237
00:10:17,950 --> 00:10:19,410
While we're at it,

238
00:10:19,450 --> 00:10:22,790
I said this is a Tadera daemon,
but it's not mine.

239
00:10:23,410 --> 00:10:25,500
Its contract is
with my predecessor.

240
00:10:25,540 --> 00:10:28,880
Maybe he meant to give it to me,
but he dipped first.

241
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:31,470
[YURU] Ah. That's why
it didn't try to help you

242
00:10:31,510 --> 00:10:32,760
when you were in danger.

243
00:10:32,800 --> 00:10:33,920
Seemed strange,

244
00:10:34,340 --> 00:10:36,600
since I've always seen daemons
try to protect their masters.

245
00:10:36,970 --> 00:10:38,180
A few years ago,

246
00:10:38,220 --> 00:10:40,600
Dad taught me all sorts of stuff
about daemons.

247
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:43,180
He said it was important
to know, just in case.

248
00:10:43,230 --> 00:10:44,230
It was tough,

249
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:46,190
since he'd only come visit us
every once in a while.

250
00:10:46,230 --> 00:10:47,610
[DERA] Mm-hmm.

251
00:10:47,810 --> 00:10:50,610
[KEN] Then he'd leave again,
sometimes without saying a word.

252
00:10:50,650 --> 00:10:51,730
That's him.

253
00:10:51,780 --> 00:10:54,070
[KEN] My mom died the other day.

254
00:10:54,530 --> 00:10:57,280
I tried to reach out,
but I couldn't get him.

255
00:10:57,660 --> 00:10:59,120
I was all alone.

256
00:11:00,280 --> 00:11:03,790
I thought I had to get stronger
so I could survive on my own.

257
00:11:03,830 --> 00:11:07,000
So I decided to contract
a couple powerful daemons.

258
00:11:07,040 --> 00:11:09,670
I found where Tenaga-Ashinaga
were sealed

259
00:11:09,710 --> 00:11:11,380
and offered them my blood,

260
00:11:11,420 --> 00:11:13,760
but they wound up
being really evil.

261
00:11:13,800 --> 00:11:15,920
At first,
I thought it would be fine,

262
00:11:15,970 --> 00:11:17,130
since as their master,

263
00:11:17,180 --> 00:11:18,800
they wouldn't be
able to hurt me.

264
00:11:18,850 --> 00:11:21,560
But no matter what I said,
they wouldn't listen.

265
00:11:21,850 --> 00:11:23,020
I freed them,

266
00:11:23,060 --> 00:11:25,230
so I knew I had to do something
to stop them

267
00:11:25,270 --> 00:11:26,350
from running rampant.

268
00:11:26,390 --> 00:11:28,230
And knowing the path
to the Lost House,

269
00:11:28,270 --> 00:11:29,900
you decided to trap them inside.

270
00:11:29,940 --> 00:11:33,440
[KEN] Right. Dad taught me
about this place a while back.

271
00:11:33,490 --> 00:11:35,860
Always wondered
why he passed this job to me

272
00:11:35,900 --> 00:11:37,820
ten years ago
almost out of nowhere.

273
00:11:37,860 --> 00:11:39,200
It was around the same time

274
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:41,200
Yuru's parents
fled from the village.

275
00:11:41,240 --> 00:11:42,740
One day, he tells me

276
00:11:42,780 --> 00:11:45,040
I have to manage
all of our work going forward,

277
00:11:45,080 --> 00:11:46,960
and then he's out the door.

278
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,750
That was the last
I heard from him.

279
00:11:49,380 --> 00:11:51,290
And now it all makes sense.

280
00:11:51,340 --> 00:11:53,710
Bastard dumped
the responsibilities on me.

281
00:11:53,750 --> 00:11:57,010
Split before anything
incriminating came his way.

282
00:11:57,510 --> 00:12:00,600
Didn't realize he had
some rugrat in another country.

283
00:12:00,640 --> 00:12:01,720
[Ken gasps]

284
00:12:01,930 --> 00:12:04,060
I guess he wanted
to keep us out of his work,

285
00:12:04,100 --> 00:12:06,060
because he didn't talk
much about it.

286
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:07,850
Sometimes he'd drink,

287
00:12:07,890 --> 00:12:09,940
and a complaint
or two would slip out.

288
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:12,770
Miss Nagisa wasn't
from the village, right?

289
00:12:13,070 --> 00:12:14,860
Since she was from down here,

290
00:12:14,900 --> 00:12:17,360
she was able to tell
my dad was the same.

291
00:12:17,490 --> 00:12:20,950
She dug into Dad's past to
find his dirty little secrets.

292
00:12:20,990 --> 00:12:22,240
Then threatened to tell everyone

293
00:12:22,280 --> 00:12:24,120
if he didn't teach her
the way out.

294
00:12:24,160 --> 00:12:25,330
He told me if I met her,

295
00:12:25,370 --> 00:12:27,370
I shouldn't trust
her kind appearance.

296
00:12:27,410 --> 00:12:29,290
She's a tigress
in sheep's clothing.

297
00:12:29,330 --> 00:12:30,380
[Yuru gasps]

298
00:12:30,420 --> 00:12:32,670
[YURU] Not bad, Mom.

299
00:12:32,710 --> 00:12:34,210
That wasn't all he said.

300
00:12:34,250 --> 00:12:37,220
He pretty openly despised
Higashi Village's traditions

301
00:12:37,260 --> 00:12:38,630
involving the twins.

302
00:12:38,670 --> 00:12:40,260
But in this case,

303
00:12:40,300 --> 00:12:42,470
all he did was teach them
how to leave.

304
00:12:42,510 --> 00:12:44,390
He didn't help them
actually escape.

305
00:12:44,430 --> 00:12:48,140
Still, that meant he defied
the will of Higashi Village.

306
00:12:48,180 --> 00:12:49,980
And he had been feuding
with the Kagemoris

307
00:12:50,020 --> 00:12:51,850
for so long at that point,

308
00:12:51,900 --> 00:12:53,400
he had nowhere to go.

309
00:12:54,070 --> 00:12:56,740
Maybe retiring
was his only option.

310
00:12:58,610 --> 00:12:59,860
[doorbell chimes]

311
00:12:59,900 --> 00:13:00,900
DANNO

312
00:13:01,110 --> 00:13:02,870
-[DERA] Sweetie, we're home.
-Is Yuru here?

313
00:13:02,910 --> 00:13:05,280
Are you okay?
What happened to your face?

314
00:13:05,330 --> 00:13:07,910
Oh, uh... It's fine.
Just a scratch.

315
00:13:07,950 --> 00:13:10,160
Sorry I didn't tell you
when I left.

316
00:13:10,210 --> 00:13:12,670
[HANA] Oh, you had me
worried sick, young man!

317
00:13:12,710 --> 00:13:14,040
But you're all right.

318
00:13:14,090 --> 00:13:15,290
I'm so relieved!

319
00:13:15,840 --> 00:13:16,920
[YURU] I can't believe

320
00:13:17,050 --> 00:13:19,420
Hana actually got this worried
about me.

321
00:13:19,470 --> 00:13:21,130
She's truly kind.

322
00:13:21,630 --> 00:13:23,760
[HANA] I am so glad
we're not gonna be wracked

323
00:13:23,800 --> 00:13:25,260
with medical bills!

324
00:13:25,600 --> 00:13:26,640
[Dera grunts]

325
00:13:27,510 --> 00:13:29,560
[HANA] Amazed
you're in one piece, Dera.

326
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:31,230
Kinda lucky
after picking a fight

327
00:13:31,270 --> 00:13:33,060
with the Kagemoris like that.

328
00:13:33,610 --> 00:13:36,650
Oh, where to begin.
Ah, I'll explain it all later.

329
00:13:36,690 --> 00:13:37,900
HORSE BETTING TICKET

330
00:13:37,940 --> 00:13:40,280
-Let me crash for a few minutes.
-[rustling]

331
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:41,360
Uh?

332
00:13:41,990 --> 00:13:43,490
[HANA] Gambling?

333
00:13:43,530 --> 00:13:45,070
Fooling around?

334
00:13:45,120 --> 00:13:46,240
[Dera stammers]

335
00:13:46,280 --> 00:13:48,290
[KEN] Hello, nice to meet you.

336
00:13:48,330 --> 00:13:50,370
My name is Ken Tadera.

337
00:13:50,410 --> 00:13:52,330
Thank you for welcoming me
into your home.

338
00:13:52,370 --> 00:13:54,170
Tadera?

339
00:13:55,630 --> 00:13:57,340
A love child?

340
00:13:57,840 --> 00:14:00,670
Off the top of your head,
what's the value of your assets?

341
00:14:00,720 --> 00:14:03,680
Oh, no! Calculating
the divorce settlement already?

342
00:14:03,720 --> 00:14:05,720
I'm dead broke,
and my only assets are

343
00:14:05,760 --> 00:14:06,970
some land and a house.

344
00:14:07,010 --> 00:14:09,140
Sadly, both of those
are Tadera clan daemons,

345
00:14:09,180 --> 00:14:10,890
so you won't get them
if we split up!

346
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:15,560
[HANA] Daemons you have
to pay property taxes on?

347
00:14:15,610 --> 00:14:17,900
DAEMONS OF THE SHADOW REALM

348
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:23,860
[HANA] Hi everyone!
My name is Hana Danno!

349
00:14:23,900 --> 00:14:27,070
I work as a retainer
and runner for Higashi Village.

350
00:14:27,120 --> 00:14:30,120
I live down the mountain
with my cute little fur babies!

351
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:32,500
But things took
a turn for the worse!

352
00:14:32,540 --> 00:14:34,040
Dera, my kinda boss,

353
00:14:34,080 --> 00:14:36,080
strongarmed me
into marrying him!

354
00:14:36,130 --> 00:14:37,840
[Dera laughs]

355
00:14:37,880 --> 00:14:41,460
[HANA] But my heart will always
belong to you, Jason Statham!

356
00:14:41,510 --> 00:14:44,510
What's more, he's helping
a kid with serious baggage!

357
00:14:44,550 --> 00:14:46,340
Plus there's his own.

358
00:14:46,390 --> 00:14:50,220
The gambling! The infidelity!
The worthless real estate!

359
00:14:50,260 --> 00:14:51,520
And worst of all...

360
00:14:51,560 --> 00:14:53,480
His secret love child!

361
00:14:53,520 --> 00:14:56,100
Every day's another
exciting development

362
00:14:56,140 --> 00:14:59,320
in the life of the beautiful,
young newlywed Hana Danno.

363
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:02,440
I've been trying to tell you,
the kid doesn't belong to me.

364
00:15:03,530 --> 00:15:05,360
[HANA] Okay, let's sum it up.

365
00:15:05,400 --> 00:15:07,990
You used Left and Right
to try and find your parents,

366
00:15:08,030 --> 00:15:09,280
but thought you saw your sister,

367
00:15:09,330 --> 00:15:11,160
and got dragged off
to Kagemori manor

368
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:12,660
to reunite with her for real.

369
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:14,250
Then, you helped them deal

370
00:15:14,290 --> 00:15:16,540
with a third-party
kidnapping attempt.

371
00:15:16,580 --> 00:15:19,590
And the Kagemori clan head
provided breakfast.

372
00:15:19,630 --> 00:15:21,670
And on the way home,
you gambled, womanized,

373
00:15:21,710 --> 00:15:23,300
and picked up your love child.

374
00:15:23,340 --> 00:15:25,970
[DERA] Those last two
weren't true. I swear!

375
00:15:26,010 --> 00:15:28,550
But I'm not hearing you
deny you went gambling.

376
00:15:28,600 --> 00:15:29,640
[DERA] I will not.

377
00:15:29,680 --> 00:15:31,850
The previous clan head
never bothered

378
00:15:31,890 --> 00:15:33,430
to tell me the kid existed.

379
00:15:33,470 --> 00:15:35,230
He's not my secret love child.

380
00:15:35,270 --> 00:15:36,270
[YURU] Your father cheated?

381
00:15:36,310 --> 00:15:37,980
Don't just ask that, Yuru.

382
00:15:38,020 --> 00:15:40,150
[DERA] The old man
and my ma called it quits

383
00:15:40,190 --> 00:15:42,110
way before Ken here was born.

384
00:15:42,150 --> 00:15:44,780
The kid's mom was
probably his legal wife.

385
00:15:45,190 --> 00:15:47,950
Not like any of us have a right
to judge him for it, anyway.

386
00:15:48,410 --> 00:15:49,740
[YURU] On that note...

387
00:15:49,950 --> 00:15:52,490
I think our family should
take Ken in for a little while.

388
00:15:52,530 --> 00:15:53,750
Oh, you would!

389
00:15:53,790 --> 00:15:56,080
[DERA] Come on, he's got
nowhere else to go!

390
00:15:56,120 --> 00:15:57,830
Don't you feel sorry for him?

391
00:15:57,870 --> 00:16:00,210
[HANA] I do not,
and will never, like kids!

392
00:16:00,250 --> 00:16:02,340
Don't add another one
like it's no big deal!

393
00:16:02,380 --> 00:16:05,210
I've been told that many hands
make light work.

394
00:16:05,260 --> 00:16:06,720
And all children are a treasure.

395
00:16:06,760 --> 00:16:09,090
Well, I love Japan's
declining birthrate!

396
00:16:09,130 --> 00:16:10,800
And don't break
child labor laws!

397
00:16:11,300 --> 00:16:12,970
Plus, we barely know this kid.

398
00:16:13,010 --> 00:16:15,270
How can we trust
he's not a spy from our enemies?

399
00:16:15,310 --> 00:16:16,810
He's safe for sure.

400
00:16:16,850 --> 00:16:18,850
I don't detect
a shred of bloodlust.

401
00:16:18,890 --> 00:16:20,480
-[Kotetsu meows]
-[Hana sighs]

402
00:16:20,520 --> 00:16:22,860
[HANA] Time for a quick lesson.

403
00:16:22,900 --> 00:16:26,150
You can't just judge people
off of vibes alone.

404
00:16:26,900 --> 00:16:28,240
For example...

405
00:16:28,530 --> 00:16:29,780
[YURU] Mm?

406
00:16:29,820 --> 00:16:32,070
[Yuru grunting]

407
00:16:32,120 --> 00:16:34,030
[HANA] Consider me, now.

408
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:36,790
There's no part of me
that wants to kill you.

409
00:16:36,830 --> 00:16:39,460
But what would you do
if I changed my mind?

410
00:16:39,500 --> 00:16:40,830
Too late to escape

411
00:16:40,880 --> 00:16:41,920
-at this point.
-[Yuru chokes]

412
00:16:42,080 --> 00:16:44,460
Hey, honey?
Please, no domestic violence.

413
00:16:44,500 --> 00:16:45,880
[HANA] 'Kay.

414
00:16:45,920 --> 00:16:47,880
[Ken trembling]

415
00:16:48,170 --> 00:16:49,680
[DERA] That was a good lesson!

416
00:16:49,720 --> 00:16:50,720
You just learned

417
00:16:50,880 --> 00:16:52,390
Hana's the scariest person
in this house

418
00:16:52,430 --> 00:16:53,550
when she gets angry.

419
00:16:53,600 --> 00:16:55,010
And that's my wife!

420
00:16:55,050 --> 00:16:56,560
You've known that all along,

421
00:16:56,600 --> 00:16:58,640
and still every day
you choose to poke the bear.

422
00:16:58,680 --> 00:17:01,520
[KEN] You guys are way scarier
than I was expecting.

423
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:03,610
Is everyone
with the village like this?

424
00:17:03,650 --> 00:17:05,400
[HANA] Maybe
I shouldn't be saying this,

425
00:17:05,440 --> 00:17:07,820
but no normal person
would be caught dead

426
00:17:07,860 --> 00:17:09,610
associating
with Higashi Village.

427
00:17:09,650 --> 00:17:10,780
[Ken gasps]

428
00:17:10,820 --> 00:17:12,700
Even if the pup
is after our heads,

429
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:14,370
he would pose us nary a threat.

430
00:17:14,410 --> 00:17:16,330
Our numbers should
prove insurmountable

431
00:17:16,370 --> 00:17:17,580
for someone his age.

432
00:17:17,620 --> 00:17:19,620
Well, yeah. I suppose.

433
00:17:19,660 --> 00:17:21,210
Anyway...

434
00:17:21,250 --> 00:17:23,840
My mom fixed this up for me
before she passed away.

435
00:17:24,420 --> 00:17:27,170
Please, use it to help cover
living expenses.

436
00:17:27,210 --> 00:17:28,300
[HANA] A bank book?

437
00:17:28,340 --> 00:17:29,760
[YURU] Bank book?

438
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:32,050
[DERA] Think a ledger
for keeping track of your gold.

439
00:17:32,090 --> 00:17:33,220
Sort of.

440
00:17:33,340 --> 00:17:36,050
[Hana groans] It hasn't been
updated in years,

441
00:17:36,100 --> 00:17:38,850
so we don't know
what the actual balance is.

442
00:17:38,890 --> 00:17:40,980
Here, Dera. Take care of it.

443
00:17:41,020 --> 00:17:42,270
On it!

444
00:17:43,140 --> 00:17:45,440
Go ahead and pick up dinner
while you're out!

445
00:17:45,480 --> 00:17:46,980
[DERA] Yes, ma'am!

446
00:17:47,980 --> 00:17:49,610
[YURU] Watching her
boss around her boss

447
00:17:49,650 --> 00:17:52,150
feels like watching
a mouse eat a snake.

448
00:17:53,110 --> 00:17:54,200
[door opens]

449
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:55,910
-[DERA] I'm back.
-[door closes]

450
00:17:55,950 --> 00:17:58,580
Hey, honey?
I think you're gonna agree

451
00:17:58,620 --> 00:18:00,450
we should look after Ken
for a little while.

452
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:01,830
What?

453
00:18:04,630 --> 00:18:06,130
[Hana gasps]

454
00:18:06,670 --> 00:18:08,840
[HANA] Ken, sweetie,
are you a citizen here?

455
00:18:08,880 --> 00:18:11,800
Of course. I've been registered
for a while now, thankfully.

456
00:18:11,840 --> 00:18:13,930
[HANA]
Then on behalf of all of us,

457
00:18:13,970 --> 00:18:15,600
I'd like to welcome you
to our family!

458
00:18:15,640 --> 00:18:17,640
Thank you so much! [cries]

459
00:18:18,600 --> 00:18:19,560
[Hana grunts]

460
00:18:19,600 --> 00:18:22,350
[HANA]
Why is this kid so loaded?

461
00:18:22,390 --> 00:18:24,640
A child does not need
this much money!

462
00:18:24,690 --> 00:18:27,610
[DERA] I agree
the balance is crazy, but look.

463
00:18:27,650 --> 00:18:29,900
There are monthly deposits here.

464
00:18:29,940 --> 00:18:31,820
He's paying child support.

465
00:18:31,860 --> 00:18:33,240
A man of principles!

466
00:18:33,280 --> 00:18:35,820
You should be so proud!
What a stand-up guy!

467
00:18:35,870 --> 00:18:36,990
[DERA] Like hell he is!

468
00:18:37,030 --> 00:18:39,450
I gotta remind you
what he left me with?

469
00:18:39,490 --> 00:18:40,870
Check it.

470
00:18:41,290 --> 00:18:43,580
This last deposit
is pretty recent.

471
00:18:43,620 --> 00:18:45,000
Good news for you.

472
00:18:45,040 --> 00:18:46,630
Means he's still alive
and kickin'.

473
00:18:46,670 --> 00:18:48,840
-That's awesome!
-Then we should go look for him!

474
00:18:48,880 --> 00:18:51,380
All right, but where to start?

475
00:18:51,920 --> 00:18:54,550
Hey, Ken, do you have
any photos of him?

476
00:18:54,590 --> 00:18:57,390
Mm, no, he'd never
let me take any.

477
00:18:57,890 --> 00:18:59,600
He was a private man.

478
00:18:59,640 --> 00:19:02,600
Yeah, I'm aware.
I'm in the exact same boat.

479
00:19:02,640 --> 00:19:04,770
Don't have anything
showing his face.

480
00:19:04,810 --> 00:19:05,940
Who are we supposed to ask

481
00:19:05,980 --> 00:19:08,110
if we don't even have
a picture to show?

482
00:19:08,150 --> 00:19:09,480
Seeing how you operate,

483
00:19:09,520 --> 00:19:11,440
I'm sure he has
a million aliases.

484
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:13,650
We could try to find
someone who knew him

485
00:19:13,690 --> 00:19:14,780
through Ken's mother.

486
00:19:15,030 --> 00:19:17,410
Sorry. Before she passed,
my mom worked at a bar

487
00:19:17,450 --> 00:19:18,700
in Katsushika, Tokyo.

488
00:19:18,740 --> 00:19:20,160
I already tried.

489
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:22,580
I talked to every one
of her friends from her job.

490
00:19:22,620 --> 00:19:24,370
Asked them if they knew
where my dad was,

491
00:19:24,410 --> 00:19:25,870
and I got the same reply.

492
00:19:25,910 --> 00:19:28,750
Gonna go out on a limb here
and say no one knew a thing?

493
00:19:28,790 --> 00:19:30,800
-[KEN] Yeah.
-[Dera sighs]

494
00:19:30,840 --> 00:19:32,960
[DERA] No wonder the Kagemoris
couldn't catch him

495
00:19:33,010 --> 00:19:35,010
if his two sons can't manage.

496
00:19:35,050 --> 00:19:36,260
Eh, it's fine.

497
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:38,140
We'll have to ask
the Higashi Village folks

498
00:19:38,180 --> 00:19:40,550
and see if we can get any
roundabout leads through them.

499
00:19:40,600 --> 00:19:42,890
Not my bake sale,
not my brownies.

500
00:19:42,930 --> 00:19:45,100
You wanna do that,
you can handle it alone.

501
00:19:45,140 --> 00:19:46,480
Yeah, yeah, I know.

502
00:19:46,980 --> 00:19:49,560
You kids let the grownups
handle the details.

503
00:19:49,610 --> 00:19:50,860
Time to eat your dinner.

504
00:19:50,900 --> 00:19:53,030
And wash that grime off
before you go to bed!

505
00:19:53,070 --> 00:19:54,650
-[KEN] Okay.
-[YURU] Okay.

506
00:19:56,820 --> 00:19:59,410
[Yuru exclaims]
How can they afford

507
00:19:59,450 --> 00:20:01,830
to let me use this much water
all by myself?

508
00:20:01,870 --> 00:20:03,620
I feel like I'm doing
something wrong!

509
00:20:03,660 --> 00:20:04,790
GREW UP IN THE MOUNTAINS,
WHERE WATER IS PRECIOUS

510
00:20:14,800 --> 00:20:16,010
[KEN] Yuru?

511
00:20:16,090 --> 00:20:18,420
Are you all right
sleeping on that flat futon?

512
00:20:18,470 --> 00:20:21,850
Bedding down here's too soft
compared to what I'm used to.

513
00:20:22,600 --> 00:20:25,640
If you're sure, I feel bad
for taking the better futon

514
00:20:25,680 --> 00:20:27,890
when I'm nothing
but a freeloader in your house.

515
00:20:27,930 --> 00:20:29,270
You're part of Dera's clan,

516
00:20:29,310 --> 00:20:31,730
so you're basically family
as far as I'm concerned.

517
00:20:31,770 --> 00:20:34,360
-Make yourself at home, Ken.
-Okay.

518
00:20:34,860 --> 00:20:36,230
For what it's worth,

519
00:20:36,280 --> 00:20:38,360
I hope we find your dad
before long.

520
00:20:38,820 --> 00:20:39,780
Me too.

521
00:20:39,820 --> 00:20:41,620
He might not know...

522
00:20:41,660 --> 00:20:43,660
about my mom's passing,
I mean.

523
00:20:44,740 --> 00:20:45,950
[YURU] Hm.

524
00:20:47,830 --> 00:20:50,370
[Ken cries softly]

525
00:20:54,750 --> 00:20:56,090
[YURU] Hm?

526
00:21:00,090 --> 00:21:02,390
And for whatever
it's worth, Yuru...

527
00:21:03,100 --> 00:21:05,180
I hope we find
your parents, too.

528
00:21:05,220 --> 00:21:06,640
[continues crying]

529
00:21:08,640 --> 00:21:10,140
♪

530
00:21:15,400 --> 00:21:16,690
[door opens]

531
00:21:17,360 --> 00:21:18,440
[door closes]

532
00:21:20,150 --> 00:21:21,400
What's in the vase?

533
00:21:21,450 --> 00:21:23,820
Ken's mom's remains, apparently.

534
00:21:23,870 --> 00:21:26,280
He hasn't found a good spot
to lay her to rest.

535
00:21:26,330 --> 00:21:27,870
Man, that's gotta be rough.

536
00:21:27,910 --> 00:21:29,330
[Dera gulping]

537
00:21:29,910 --> 00:21:32,210
-[Jiro whines]
-[Kotetsu meows]

538
00:21:32,250 --> 00:21:34,670
[HANA] Well, we should check
with Ken in the morning.

539
00:21:34,710 --> 00:21:37,840
If he wants, we could make
a grave for her on my mountain.

540
00:21:37,880 --> 00:21:41,300
In character.
Little miss Gravedigger.

541
00:21:41,340 --> 00:21:43,550
[HANA] Just tell me
when it's your turn.

542
00:21:43,590 --> 00:21:45,300
I'll put you six feet under.

543
00:21:45,350 --> 00:21:46,970
-[Dera chuckles]
-[door opens]

544
00:21:47,510 --> 00:21:49,890
-[HANA] Good night, Dera.
-[door closes]

545
00:21:50,430 --> 00:21:51,680
[Dera sighs]

546
00:21:52,020 --> 00:21:53,350
[DERA] Good night.

547
00:21:54,810 --> 00:21:56,900
[♪ closing theme song playing]

548
00:23:25,860 --> 00:23:27,780
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

549
00:23:27,820 --> 00:23:29,910
[ASA] I'm glad I got to hear
your voice.

550
00:23:29,950 --> 00:23:32,790
[JIN] There actually
are faint lines visible here.

551
00:23:32,830 --> 00:23:34,750
It wasn't made
by a simple razor.

552
00:23:34,790 --> 00:23:36,790
[ASUMA] Uncle! Hello.

553
00:23:36,830 --> 00:23:39,920
EPISODE 12
RETAINER AND SHAMAN
